  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A solid sphere made out of metal&nbsp;having a bulk modulus of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>11</mn></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi>Nm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;is charged uniformly to&nbsp;a surface charge density <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msqrt><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi>Cm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is the permittivity of free space and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi></math>&nbsp;(magnitude = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>) is a positive constant of appropriate dimensions. If the volume strain produced in the sphere after charging is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></msup></math>, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;is</p>\r",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "0.25",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Bulk modulus is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mrow><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>V</mi></mrow><mi>V</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mfrac></math></p><p>The outward electrostatic pressure is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>electrostatic</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>&#963;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>P</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>V</mi></mrow><mi>V</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><msup><mi>&#963;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>B</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>V</mi></mrow><mi>V</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><msup><mfenced><msqrt><mi>&#945;</mi><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msqrt></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>11</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></msup></math></p>",
